      "id": 1,
      "text": "Franklin was founded by Mormon pioneers led by Thomas S. in 1860.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        3
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Franklin%2C_Idaho",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Franklin is named after Apostle Franklin Richards, not Benjamin Franklin, making it the only Franklin County in the U.S. not named after Benjamin Franklin.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        4,
        6
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia",
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Franklin%2C_Idaho",
      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The town’s historic buildings, dating back to 1872, include the Lorenzo Hill Hatch House and the Franklin Co‑operative Mercantile Institution, preserved by the Idaho State Historical Society.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        19
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://history.idaho.gov/franklin/",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Franklin’s early railroad history began in 1878 when the Utah Northern Railroad made the town a division point, giving it a riotous beginning as a terminus.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        12,
        13
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.franklincountyidaho.org/explore/about.php",
      "category": "transport",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Parts of the 2004 comedy film Napoleon Dynamite were filmed near Franklin, with chicken‑farm scenes shot on Ritewood Egg Farms.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        16,
        17
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Franklin%2C_Idaho",
      "category": "culture",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 6,
      "text": "Travelers along the Pioneer Byway can explore Franklin’s historic properties, offering a comprehensive overview of the region’s history.",
